WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:25.320
And it's Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

9
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.840
It's Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

10
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.280
And we are here to talk to you this week about the job.
这周我们在这里要和大家聊聊《工作》这一集。

11
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.200
Yes.
没错。

12
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.460
It's the end of season three, Angela.
安吉拉，这是第三季的结尾了。

13
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.520
This is the season three finale.
这是第三季的大结局。

14
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.120
I can't believe we're already at the season three finale.
真不敢相信我们已经聊到第三季大结局了。

15
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.120
I can't either.
我也不敢相信。

16
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.060
I can't either.
我也不敢相信。

17
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.620
I was saying to my husband the other day, I was like, babe, Jenna and I have talked for a year now about the show.
前几天我跟我丈夫说，我说，亲爱的，我和珍娜聊这部剧已经聊了一年了。

18
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.340
And it doesn't even feel like any time has gone by.
感觉时间好像还没过去多久一样。

19
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.040
I mean, I think we just really enjoy hanging out and talking with each other and also talking about the show.
我是说，我觉得我们真的很享受在一起聊天，也享受谈论这部剧的过程。

20
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.920
Well, this is actually the job part one.
嗯，这一集其实是《工作》的上半部分。

21
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:10.740
This is an hour-long episode finale, so we're dividing it into two episodes of Office Ladies so that we can really cover everything.
这是一集时长一小时的大结局，所以我们把它拆分成两期《办公室女士》来聊，这样我们才能真正把所有细节都讲透。

22
00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.440
This was written by Paul Lieberstein and Mike Shore and directed by Ken Kwapis.
这一集由保罗·利伯斯坦和迈克·肖尔编剧，肯·卡皮斯执导。

23
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.140
Jenna, do you know it was also co-edited?
珍娜，你知道它还有联合剪辑吗？

24
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.600
Not only co-written, but it was co-edited with Dave Rogers and Dean Holland.
不仅是联合编剧，它还由戴夫·罗杰斯和迪恩·霍兰德联合剪辑。

25
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.340
Wow.
哇。

26
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.820
Because it was such a big episode.
因为这一集太重要了。

27
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.660
We put everyone on this.
我们动用了所有人。

28
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.960
All hands on deck.
全员出动。

29
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.400
Well, here is a summary for part one.
好了，这是上半部分的剧情梗概。

30
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:42.920
Before leaving for his interview and confident he already has a new job at corporate, Michael names Dwight as his replacement at Dunder Mifflin Scranton.
在去参加面试前，迈克尔自信满满地认为自己已经拿到了总公司的工作，于是他任命德怀特为他在邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司的接班人。

31
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.820
Angela could not be more excited.
安吉拉对此兴奋不已。

32
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:46.460
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

33
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.400
But before Michael can leave, Jan pays a surprise visit.
但在迈克尔离开之前，简突然造访。

34
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.160
She shows Michael her new breast enhancement and says she wants to get back together.
她向迈克尔展示了她刚做的隆胸手术，并表示想和他复合。

35
00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.960
Jim and Karen leave early as they are also interviewing for the job at corporate.
吉姆和凯伦提前离开了，因为他们也要去总公司面试那个职位。

36
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:10.380
Dwight makes Andy his number two since Andy is the only person who would interview for the position.
德怀特任命安迪为他的二把手，因为安迪是唯一一个愿意来面试这个职位的人。

37
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.040
And that's just the first half.
而这仅仅是上半部分。

38
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.320
There's more to come.
后面还有更多精彩内容。

39
00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:14.660
Yeah.
没错。

40
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.300
Well, listen, to kick off this finale episode, we have a surprise gueSt.
好了，听着，为了开启这集大结局，我们请到了一位惊喜嘉宾。

41
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.680
We're so excited.
我们太激动了。

42
00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.980
Writer, Toby himself, Paul Lieberstein.
编剧，也就是托比本人，保罗·利伯斯坦。

43
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.560
Toby is in the house.
托比来了。

44
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.140
Well, you know, in the Zoom house.
嗯，你知道，是在Zoom里来了。

45
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.780
Toby's in the Zoom house.
托比在Zoom里来了。

46
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.700
Oh, well, we asked him all about being Toby and all about this episode.
哦，我们问了他所有关于扮演托比以及关于这一集的问题。

47
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.620
Sam, will you play the interview?
萨姆，能播放一下采访录音吗？

48
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.290
Oh, Paul Lieberstein.
哦，保罗·利伯斯坦。

49
00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.030
Welcome to Office Lady.
欢迎来到《办公室女士》。

50
00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.790
Hello, Jenna Fisher.
你好，珍娜·费舍尔。

51
00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.630
Hello, Angela Kinsey.
你好，安吉拉·金赛。

52
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:52.890
Thank you for having me.
谢谢你邀请我。

53
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.850
Oh, thanks so much for being on.
噢，非常感谢你能来。

54
00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:55.790
My pleasure.
这是我的荣幸。

55
00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.850
We're so excited to have you today.
我们今天能请到你真是太兴奋了。

56
00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:58.830
Thank you.
谢谢。

57
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.390
I'm excited to be here.
我也很高兴能来到这里。

58
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.110
Good.
太好了。

59
00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:05.250
We were texting, and I know you were texting with Angela as well.
我们之前发过短信，我知道你也和安吉拉发过短信。

60
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:13.290
And you told us that you have not seen an episode of the show since it aired, but that you were
你告诉我们，自从剧集播出后你就没再看过，但你今天

61
00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.090
going to watch the job today.
打算看这一集。

62
00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.070
How was that experience for you?
那次体验对你来说感觉如何？

63
00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:17.810
I'm dying to know.
我太想知道了。

64
00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.550
It was really interesting.
真的很有趣。

65
00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.970
I felt like there's moments that really, really shined.
我觉得有些时刻真的很棒，非常出彩。

66
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.230
And then there's like, you know, the writer part of me was like, oh, okay, I think I would have done that a little differently now.
然后，你知道的，我作为编剧的那部分会想：噢，好吧，我觉得现在我会换种方式来处理。

67
00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.070
But I didn't think there was anything that was embarrassing.
但我并不觉得有什么令人尴尬的地方。

68
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.210
No.
没有。

69
00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.310
Look on yourself.
对自己宽容点。

70
00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.690
This is an amazing, delightful episode.
这是一集非常棒、非常令人愉快的剧集。

71
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:52.990
I know you, and you're such an amazing writer, and I can see you watching things through the filter of like, oh, and you're a producer, and you direct.
我了解你，你是一位如此出色的编剧，我能看出你在观看时会带着某种滤镜，毕竟你还是制片人，也参与导演工作。

72
00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:56.430
So I imagine you're watching it through all those different layers.
所以我猜你在看的时候会考虑到所有这些不同的层面。

73
00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.370
Yeah.
是啊。

74
00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.930
Yeah, you know, there's everything.
是啊，你知道，什么都有。

75
00:03:59.090 --> 00:03:59.810
It's like framing.
比如构图。

76
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.710
It's like, oh, I should be in front of, oh.
或者会想：噢，我应该站在前面，噢。

77
00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.870
Or that was repetitive.
或者觉得那段重复了。

78
00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.970
We already said that.
我们已经说过那句话了。

79
00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:05.670
Paul.
保罗。

80
00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.990
We didn't need to do it again.
我们没必要再来一遍。

81
00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.470
But then I get really impressed with some other stuff.
但随后我又会被其他一些东西深深打动。

82
00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:16.570
Well, we do always like to start by asking people how they came to be on The Office.
嗯，我们总是喜欢先问问大家是如何加入《办公室》剧组的。

83
00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:21.590
You are one of our original writers, and you were with us the entire nine seasons.
你是我们的元老级编剧之一，而且整整九季都和我们在一起。

84
00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.670
You were our showrunner as well for a period of time.
你还曾有一段时间担任过我们的剧集运作人。

85
00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.890
How did it come about that you were on the show?
你是怎么加入这部剧的呢？

86
00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:34.650
Well, I had worked with Greg Daniels before and known him a very long time.
嗯，我之前和格雷格·丹尼尔斯合作过，认识他很久了。

87
00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.090
And we did King of the Hill together.
我们一起做过《山丘之王》。

88
00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:41.050
And when they started the show, I stopped by the pilot.
当他们开始筹备这部剧时，我顺道去看了试播集的拍摄。

89
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.930
You know, I had nothing to do with the pilot, but I stopped by a few days.
你知道，我跟试播集没什么关系，但我去现场待了几天。

90
00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:48.270
And it was, I just kind of loved what was happening.
当时，我简直爱上了正在发生的一切。

91
00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.830
And it was, you know, I loved the British.
而且，你知道，我喜欢英版的那种风格。

92
00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:58.510
And so then when it got picked up, I was psyched that he asked me to come on.
所以当剧集被预订后，他邀请我加入时，我感到非常兴奋。

93
00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:05.650
So there's just like kind of a very traditional thing that writers and actors are kind of separating on a TV show.
当时电视圈有一种非常传统的做法，就是编剧和演员是分开的。

94
00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.830
You know, and they're kind of asked not to talk.
你知道，他们通常被要求不要交流。

95
00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:15.190
And he, at this point, was questioning a lot of those, like, rules and why is this happening?
而他在当时就在质疑很多这样的规则，比如为什么要这样？

96
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.210
And does this really make a better TV show?
这真的能让电视节目变得更好吗？

97
00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:22.810
So we talked about roles for, it was Mindy and BJ and myself and Mike.
所以我们讨论了角色分配，当时有敏迪、BJ、我还有迈克。

98
00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.090
And then there was a couple of consultants.
还有几位顾问。

99
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.470
There was Lester and Larry.
莱斯特和拉里。

100
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.090
So the four of us each got, like, little roles.
所以我们四个人每人都得到了一些小角色。

101
00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.730
I guess Mike's didn't come on.
我猜迈克的那部分没播出来。

102
00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.910
Most didn't start that season.
那一季大多数都没开始。

103
00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:45.810
But so we had talked about just doing a little thing to kind of have the experience of being an actor.
所以我们讨论过只是做点小事，体验一下当演员的感觉。

104
00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.890
And hopefully it would inform our writing.
希望这能为我们的写作提供灵感。

105
00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.610
So here he wanted to kind of, like, break that down together.
所以他想在这里一起把那个拆解开来。

106
00:05:52.850 --> 00:06:01.530
So I feel like I'm not sure how Toey happened, but I feel like I left the room and I came back and they said, you're going to play this part.
我不确定托比这个角色是怎么来的，但我感觉我离开房间再回来时，他们就说，你要演这个角色。

107
00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:10.050
And it was one line, you know, in Diversity Day about, you know, I say this one line and get kicked out of the room.
那只有一句台词，你知道，在《多元化日》那一集里，我说了那一句台词就被赶出了房间。

108
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:19.590
Now, I heard, Paul, and you tell me if this is true, I heard that at the table read, they had you read that line and that Steve, as Michael,
现在，我听说，保罗，你告诉我这是不是真的，我听说在剧本围读会上，他们让你读那句台词，然后史蒂夫，作为迈克尔，

109
00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.710
jumped on you so viciously and everyone erupted in laughter.
非常凶猛地扑向你，大家都哄堂大笑。

110
00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:32.350
Because you sort of almost reacted a little bit as yourself and a little bit maybe how you thought Tobey might, you know, but you still didn't know who Tobey was at that moment,
因为你当时的反应有点像你自己，也有点像你觉得托比可能会有的反应，你知道，但你当时还不知道托比是谁，

111
00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:32.610
right?
对吧？

112
00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.430
You're still discovering who is Tobey.
你还在探索托比到底是谁。

113
00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:43.370
There were early table reads where it was just, for, like, weird contractual reasons, just the main five actors.
早期的剧本围读会，因为一些奇怪的合同原因，只有主要的五位演员参加。

114
00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.550
And I was reading Kevin.
当时我在读凯文的台词。

115
00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.670
Yeah, you read a few roles.
没错，你读过好几个角色。

116
00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:48.230
Yeah.
是的。

117
00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.950
And I think I did well.
我觉得我表现得不错。

118
00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.430
I think I got laughs as Kevin.
我觉得我演凯文时逗笑了大家。

119
00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:57.810
I think that the supporting cast wasn't there because you were guest stars and you were not series regular.
我想配角没去是因为你们是客串明星，不是常规演员。

120
00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:01.650
So in a series regular contract, you're required to do the table read.
因为在常规演员合同里，你是必须参加剧本围读的。

121
00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.070
It's part of your acting deal.
这是你表演协议的一部分。

122
00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.910
But I think they have to pay you more.
但我觉得他们必须多付你钱。

123
00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.630
Oh, to attend those?
哦，参加那些围读吗？

124
00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.030
If you don't have that kind of contract.
如果你没有那种合同的话。

125
00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:12.230
That sounds right.
听起来确实如此。

126
00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:12.730
Yeah.
是的。

127
00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:17.330
You know, it's interesting because I, as a guest star, they say you're invited.
你知道，这很有趣，因为作为客串明星，他们会说你是受邀参加的。

128
00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:17.910
Yeah.
没错。

129
00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:18.270
Right?
对吧？

130
00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.330
Not required.
不是必须的。

131
00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.430
You're invited if you would like to come.
如果你想来，你是受邀的。

132
00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.250
And I always do.
我总是会去。

133
00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.770
But I think you're right, Jenna.
但我觉得你说得对，珍娜。

134
00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:26.990
It wasn't until after Boo's Cruise that we started coming to table reads.
直到《布的游轮》之后，我们才开始参加剧本围读会。

135
00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:27.770
Yeah.
是的。

136
00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:33.610
So, Paul, you read a bunch of roles and everyone laughed when Michael jumped on you as Toby.
所以，保罗，你读了很多角色，当迈克尔作为托比扑向你时，大家都笑了。

137
00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.470
And I feel like that helped seal the deal.
我觉得这有助于敲定这个角色。

138
00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:37.930
But we also didn't expect that part to come back ever.
但我们也从没想过这个角色会再出现。

139
00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:39.830
Oh, that's how they got you.
哦，他们就是这样套住你的。

140
00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.170
That's what Mike Schur said about Moe's.
迈克·舒尔就是这么说莫斯的。

141
00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.190
It was just supposed to be a silly photo, you know?
那本来只是张愚蠢的照片，你知道吗？

142
00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:46.890
Yeah.
是的。

143
00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:47.330
Yeah.
没错。

144
00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:47.830
That's right.
确实如此。

145
00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.010
He started as a photo.
他最初只是张照片。

146
00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:57.910
And then years later, he had to walk around with that beard for like a whole year, a whole season, because Greg wouldn't let him use a fake one.
然后几年后，他不得不留着那把胡子整整一年，整整一季，因为格雷格不让他用假胡子。

147
00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.610
And it all started because he was just going to be in a photo.
而这一切的开始，仅仅是因为他要出现在一张照片里。

148
00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.150
And then the fake one looked better, I think.
而且我觉得假胡子看起来效果更好。

149
00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:04.750
Yes.
是的。

150
00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:10.130
And then he was furious because he had had that huge beard and the fake one worked just as well.
然后他气疯了，因为他留了那么大的胡子，而假胡子的效果其实是一样的。

151
00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.270
Well, Paul, how was that experience?
那么，保罗，那次经历感觉如何？

152
00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:16.710
Was Greg right?
格雷格说对了吗？

153
00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.750
Did you feel like you learned from the experience of being an actor?
你觉得从这次当演员的经历中学到了什么吗？

154
00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:22.330
I absolutely did.
我绝对学到了。

155
00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.890
But it took a while to get there.
但花了一段时间才领悟到。

156
00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:28.490
I don't know if you remember, but we were doing this kind of room bit about like my acting school.
不知道你还记不记得，我们当时在聊关于我表演学校的事。

157
00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:31.630
I do remember your acting school bit.
我记得你说的表演学校那段。

158
00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:32.190
It's okay.
还行吧。

159
00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.170
So imagine going into acting, knowing nothing about acting.
试想一下，你对表演一窍不通，却去学了表演。

160
00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:43.990
And the first thing you're being taught is take your water bottle off your desk and put it underneath your desk because the label isn't cleared.
你学到的第一件事竟然是：把桌上的水瓶拿走放到桌下，因为标签没经过授权。

161
00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.110
All right.
好吧。

162
00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.410
That's now the first thing I know about acting.
这就是我现在关于表演的第一认知。

163
00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:51.530
You know, and it was like things like that that made up my acting school.
你知道，就是诸如此类的事情构成了我的表演学校经历。

164
00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.410
I remember.
我记得。

165
00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:57.350
Also, I remember Rain would just ride you so hard.
我还记得雷恩当时对你要求特别严。

166
00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.510
Like, you go, hey, Kate.
比如，你说，嘿，凯特。

167
00:08:58.610 --> 00:08:59.590
And she goes, hey, Paul.
然后她说，嘿，保罗。

168
00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.270
And you're like, dang it.
你就觉得，该死。

169
00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.170
Because she was supposed to be Meredith in the moment you're in a scene.
因为在演戏的时候，她当时应该扮演梅雷迪思。

170
00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:05.670
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

171
00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.250
And I remember Rain would like tease you so hard.
我记得雷恩当时总是那样狠狠地逗你。

172
00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:11.370
Yeah.
没错。

173
00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.170
There was very little acting I was doing.
我当时其实没怎么在演戏。

174
00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.370
There was a breakthrough moment for me.
后来我迎来了一个突破性的时刻。

175
00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.690
They kept saying, talk louder.
他们一直说，大声点。

176
00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:18.990
And I wouldn't.
但我就是不肯。

177
00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:22.530
You're like, no, I'm talking to a person right here.
你当时想的是，不，我就跟眼前这个人说话。

178
00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:23.710
Why would I talk louder?
我为什么要大声说话？

179
00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.570
You just rolled out multicams for yourself, but that's okay.
你当时给自己预设了多机位拍摄的场景，不过没关系。

180
00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:29.650
Yeah.
是啊。

181
00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.330
And theater.
还有剧场表演。

182
00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:31.330
All the theater.
所有的剧场表演。

183
00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.770
And then so we were doing a kitchen scene and they kept telling me to speak up.
当时我们在拍一场厨房戏，他们一直让我大声点。

184
00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:41.890
And then Brian said, why don't you imagine like this room is artificially quiet because they turned off the refrigerator.
然后布莱恩说，你为什么不想象一下，因为冰箱关掉了，所以这个房间异常安静呢？

185
00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:42.490
Right.
对。

186
00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:43.490
Because of the sound.
因为声音的原因。

187
00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:46.270
Why don't you imagine that the refrigerator is on?
你为什么不想象一下冰箱是开着的呢？

188
00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:47.210
And you have to talk about it.
然后你得谈论这件事。

189
00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:58.650
Oh, an actor does that, you know, it put this like, and it wasn't just like one little thing.
噢，演员就是会那样做，你知道，这就像是……而且不仅仅是那一小件事。

190
00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:05.430
It was like, oh, an actor has to put all these, all those little details.
就像是，噢，演员必须把所有这些小细节都考虑进去。

191
00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:08.510
It has to justify anything that needs to be done.
必须为所有需要完成的事情找到合理的理由。

192
00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.430
They don't just do what feels real.
他们不能只是做感觉真实的事情。

193
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:14.510
They have to like find a way to do what they need to do and make it feel real.
他们必须找到一种方法，既能完成需要做的事，又能让它感觉真实。

194
00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.770
I love hearing that.
我很喜欢听这个。

195
00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.590
Is this something that you've brought to other projects?
你把这种方法带到其他项目中了吗？

196
00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:25.610
Paul, as a writer, showrunner, creator of shows, have you asked your writing staff to act at all?
保罗，作为编剧、剧集运作人、创作者，你有没有要求过你的编剧团队去演戏？

197
00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:26.430
I did.
我有过。

198
00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:27.130
Let's see.
让我想想。

199
00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:27.870
I'm ghosted.
我被无视了。

200
00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:33.450
I had Blitz's brother, Andy Blitz, and I created a part for him.
我有布里茨的兄弟，安迪·布里茨，我为他创作了一个角色。

201
00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:44.270
Well, I have to say, and Jenna and I have talked about this a lot, and we talked about this when Greg came on as well, that we loved that we got to be around the writers.
嗯，我必须得说，珍娜和我经常聊起这个，格雷格加入的时候我们也聊过，我们真的很喜欢能和编剧们待在一起。

202
00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.750
We loved when we got to go up into the writers' room.
我们很喜欢能去编剧室的感觉。

203
00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:55.070
Sometimes we would shoot over in the warehouse, and there was that back stairwell that went up where your kitchen was with your snacks, and we would come up and hang out.
有时候我们在仓库那边拍摄，那里有个后楼梯通往你们放零食的厨房，我们就会上去在那儿待着。

204
00:10:55.070 --> 00:11:07.810
And it was really fun for us to have you guys on set, and it's hard for me to imagine other shows now without that creative collaboration and that feeling of safety and truSt.
你们能来片场对我们来说真的很有趣，现在很难想象没有那种创意协作、没有那种安全感和信任感的剧组会是什么样。

205
00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:14.070
And we've all worked on other shows where it is not the case, and it's something that I really cherish.
我们都曾在其他剧组工作过，情况并非如此，所以我真的很珍惜这一点。

206
00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.110
Yeah, me too.
是啊，我也是。

207
00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:17.630
Greg was right.
格雷格说得对。

208
00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:24.390
Breaking down that wall made us understand each other a lot better, and we all worked together.
打破那堵墙让我们彼此更加了解，我们大家都是齐心协力工作的。

209
00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:31.390
Well, speaking of having to team up, for this episode, The Job, you teamed up with Mike Schur.
说到团队合作，这一集《工作》就是你和迈克·舒尔合作完成的。

210
00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:33.310
You guys co-wrote this episode.
你们俩共同编写了这一集。

211
00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.470
How did that work?
那是怎么运作的呢？

212
00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:42.290
I have kind of a memory of, you know, this was at the end of the season and a long season, and a lot of episodes are written in a different way.
我有点印象，你知道，这是季末了，这一季很长，很多剧集的编写方式都不太一样。

213
00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:49.570
So it wasn't that Mike and I went off into a room together and then came out with this show.
所以并不是迈克和我关进一个房间，然后就写出了这一集。

214
00:11:49.570 --> 00:12:04.610
I think that we both were running the process of writing this episode together, you know, and we would, we beat it all out with some writers would come in and out,
我想我们俩是一起把控这一集的编写流程的，你知道，我们会和一些进进出出的编剧一起把剧情敲定，

215
00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:10.230
but we would be the two people that was there making sure, you know, the episode was what we wanted.
但我们俩是主要负责的人，确保这一集呈现出我们想要的效果。

216
00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:15.910
And then he would go take a scene, I would take a scene, or he would take a few writers to take a scene, and I would do the same.
然后他会负责一个场景，我负责一个场景，或者他带几个编剧去写一个场景，我也一样。

217
00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.390
I think that's basically how this one worked.
我想这基本上就是这一集的运作方式。

218
00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:29.570
It's funny that you mention working in groups like that, because I remember there were times on the set where Greg would call me off set.
你提到这种小组工作方式很有趣，因为我记得在片场时，格雷格有时会把我叫出片场。

219
00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.350
He would say, Jenna, are you in the scene?
他会说，珍娜，你在这一场戏里吗？

220
00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.170
Are you in the scene?
你在这一场戏里吗？

221
00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:37.870
Okay, I've got three writers talking about Jim and Pam, I want you to sit in on that, go in there, go in there.
好吧，我有三个编剧在讨论吉姆和帕姆的事，我想让你旁听一下，进去吧，进去吧。

222
00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:39.890
Oh, my gosh, I would get so excited.
天哪，我当时会特别兴奋。

223
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.630
I would be like, oh, I can't wait.
我会觉得，噢，我等不及了。

224
00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:42.630
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

225
00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:44.690
And I mostly just listened.
我大部分时间只是在听。

226
00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.390
And sometimes I would throw out ideas.
有时候我也会提出一些想法。

227
00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:51.710
But that was so cool, because you guys would kind of divide up a script.
但这真的很酷，因为你们会把剧本分拆开来。

228
00:12:51.710 --> 00:13:00.630
And like a group of three people would go work on Dwight's stuff, and then another three people would work on some other aspect of the story,
比如一组三个人去写德怀特的部分，然后另外三个人去写故事的其他方面，

229
00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.890
at least from my little bit of experience in the writer's room.
至少以我在编剧室那点微薄的经验来看是这样的。

230
00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:13.430
Well, it was episode by episode, you know, and some came in, some were really like conceived by the writer and went straight all the way through.
嗯，这得看具体是哪一集，你知道，有些剧集确实是由某位编剧构思并从头写到尾的。

231
00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.970
And some were extremely collaborative.
而有些则非常注重协作。

232
00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:24.550
But even when a writer did it by himself or herself, there was, you know, there was tons of discussion about what was going to happen.
但即使是编剧独立完成的，你知道，关于剧情走向也会有大量的讨论。

233
00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:31.870
Well, a big storyline in this episode is that Jan and Michael get back together.
这一集里有个重头戏是简和迈克尔复合了。

234
00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.090
And Jan has had breast augmentation.
而且简还做了隆胸手术。

235
00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:39.130
And we're so curious about this storyline.
我们对这个剧情线非常好奇。

236
00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.930
Like, how did it come about?
比如，这是怎么想出来的？

237
00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.190
Did you talk to Melora about it?
你有和梅洛拉聊过这个吗？

238
00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.890
And working with Melora and Steve, what was that like?
和梅洛拉以及史蒂夫合作是什么感觉？

239
00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.810
I think there was a card on the wall for a long time that said, Jan gets a boob job.
我想墙上的卡片上写着“简做了隆胸手术”已经很久了。

240
00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:53.970
And we're kind of looking for the right place.
我们一直在寻找合适的切入点。

241
00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.090
And then so we had to break up.
然后他们不得不分手。

242
00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.550
She gets a boob job.
她做了隆胸手术。

243
00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.150
And because of that, they get back together.
正因为如此，他们又复合了。

244
00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.730
It was something that happened during cocktails.
这事儿发生在鸡尾酒会期间。

245
00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:06.430
Jan did this super long talking head on the lawn of the...
简在草坪上做了一段超长的独白……

246
00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.890
Yes, in front of David Wallace's house.
是的，在大卫·华莱士家门前。

247
00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.530
Yeah, in front of David Wallace's house.
对，在大卫·华莱士家门前。

248
00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:18.670
And in writing that, we kind of discovered how Jan was on the road to self-destruction.
在写那段戏的时候，我们算是发现了简是如何走上自我毁灭之路的。

249
00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:19.330
Yes.
没错。

250
00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.010
Like, that crystallized it for us.
那段戏让我们彻底理清了这一点。

251
00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.910
It's like, oh, she's taking herself down.
就像是，噢，她在自毁前程。

252
00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:28.610
Once we got that, this was like a stage in her spiral.
一旦我们有了那个，这就成了她堕落过程中的一个阶段。

253
00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.630
Well, it's so brilliant.
嗯，这太精彩了。

254
00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:38.910
I just thought Melora and Steve just, once again, their dynamic as Jan and Michael to me, it's juSt...
我只是觉得梅洛拉和史蒂夫，再一次，他们作为简和迈克尔的互动对我来说，简直是……

255
00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:39.250
It was so good.
太棒了。

256
00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:39.870
So good.
太棒了。

257
00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.590
I could watch them all day.
我可以看他们一整天。

258
00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:46.390
My favorite part of the episode was when she came back in for the first time.
我这集最喜欢的部分是她第一次回来的时候。

259
00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:46.990
Yeah.
是啊。

260
00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.390
And he's just looking at her.
而他只是看着她。

261
00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.230
And, Jenna, you're right there.
而且，珍娜，你就坐在那儿。

262
00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.710
And you're looking down.
你还低着头。

263
00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:54.490
Yeah.
是啊。

264
00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:56.710
He's like, why privately?
他就像是，为什么要私下里？

265
00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:57.770
Why privately?
为什么要私下里？

266
00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:03.920
He's put right in the middle of the two of them.
他被夹在他们俩中间。

267
00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.120
Yeah.
是啊。

268
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.440
It could have been just such a normal little dud of a scene.
这本来可能只是一场平淡无奇的普通戏份。

269
00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:20.020
You know, but he walked this line of being mean and trying to be polite and shocked and...
你知道，但他把握住了那种既刻薄又试图保持礼貌和震惊的界限，而且……

270
00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.280
Freaking the ass out.
简直吓坏了。

271
00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.580
Freaking out and making it all real at once.
惊慌失措，同时又让这一切显得如此真实。

272
00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.460
It was so funny to see him do that.
看他那样做真是太搞笑了。

273
00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:36.940
I have to ask you, who is responsible for Creed Thoughts?
我必须问你，是谁负责“克里德思想”的？

274
00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.160
I think that was a mic talking head.
我想那是迈克的一个采访镜头。

275
00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.860
And then Jason Kessler did it on the blog.
然后杰森·凯斯勒在博客上做了那个。

276
00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:45.920
He did a blog of Creed Thoughts on NBC.com, I guess.
我想他在NBC.com上写了一个“克里德思想”的博客。

277
00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.640
And he was your writer's assistant?
他是你们的编剧助理吗？

278
00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:48.260
Is that right?
是这样吗？

279
00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:49.040
Yeah.
是啊。

280
00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:53.340
And then he kind of took over the digital media stuff.
然后他接手了数字媒体方面的工作。

281
00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.840
I texted Creed about it this week.
我这周还给克里德发短信问了这件事。

282
00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:57.900
I was like, Creed, do you remember Creed Thoughts?
我说，克里德，你还记得“克里德思想”吗？

283
00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:58.820
Your whole blog?
你整个博客？

284
00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.300
He was like, yeah, yeah, that was fun.
他说，记得，记得，那很有趣。

285
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.500
I didn't write any of that.
我没写过那些东西。

286
