897
00:45:50.220 --> 00:45:55.060
Because you know how you were mentioning that sometimes you would check to see if you were in the background?
因为你知道你之前提到过，有时你会检查自己是否在背景里出现？

898
00:45:55.520 --> 00:45:55.680
Yeah.
是的。

899
00:45:56.880 --> 00:46:03.120
At 7 minutes, 10 seconds, Phyllis looks over her shoulder to accounting.
在7分10秒的时候，菲利斯回头看向会计部。

900
00:46:03.120 --> 00:46:08.460
And I swear that what she's doing is sneaking a look to see where the camera is.
我敢发誓，她是在偷偷看摄像机在哪里。

901
00:46:08.640 --> 00:46:15.460
And I think she thinks she's not on camera because right after that, she clicks on a website to look at fences.
我觉得她以为自己没在镜头里，因为在那之后，她立刻点开了一个网站去看栅栏。

902
00:46:15.960 --> 00:46:18.660
Yes, that's exactly what she was doing.
没错，她当时确实是在做这个。

903
00:46:18.960 --> 00:46:20.480
Yes, it was amazing.
是的，太神奇了。

904
00:46:20.820 --> 00:46:24.500
You guys, Phyllis looked at fences for like a year.
伙计们，菲利斯看栅栏看了大概有一年。

905
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:34.120
Yeah, like like for months and months trying to and we and we would, you know, she would want our opinion and we'd go over and we'd look at fences with her.
是啊，看了好几个月，她想让我们给点意见，我们就过去陪她一起看栅栏。

906
00:46:34.780 --> 00:46:36.200
Yeah, so many.
是啊，看了好多。

907
00:46:36.420 --> 00:46:36.680
It was great.
太棒了。

908
00:46:36.900 --> 00:46:37.460
So many fences.
看了好多栅栏。

909
00:46:37.800 --> 00:46:50.620
Well, now, Angela, speaking of scenes that I just absolutely love this next one with Dwight and Angela in the kitchen and Dwight is telling Angela about his new promotion.
好了，安吉拉，说到我绝对喜欢的场景，接下来这个是德怀特和安吉拉在厨房里的戏，德怀特正在告诉安吉拉他升职的事。

910
00:46:50.620 --> 00:46:52.960
He is going to have Michael's job.
他要接替迈克尔的工作了。

911
00:46:54.460 --> 00:46:55.980
Oh, it's so good.
哦，这太棒了。

912
00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:56.740
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

913
00:46:56.900 --> 00:47:00.260
It's one of these Shakespearean moments between Dwight and Angela.
这是德怀特和安吉拉之间莎士比亚式的时刻之一。

914
00:47:00.840 --> 00:47:02.000
Very Macbeth, right?
很有《麦克白》的感觉，对吧？

915
00:47:02.420 --> 00:47:08.660
And once again, they're not facing each other, you know, so Angela doesn't even see his face.
而且再一次，他们没有面对面，所以安吉拉甚至没看到他的表情。

916
00:47:09.060 --> 00:47:14.860
And at the end, Angela, you say goodbye, Kelly Kapoor.
最后，安吉拉，你说了一句“再见，凯莉·卡普尔”。

917
00:47:15.460 --> 00:47:15.860
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

918
00:47:16.020 --> 00:47:17.980
And that was not in the script, lady.
那句台词剧本里可没有，女士。

919
00:47:18.380 --> 00:47:19.220
I know.
我知道。

920
00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:19.720
I know.
我知道。

921
00:47:19.900 --> 00:47:22.800
So so I got to improvise a little bit right there.
所以我当时即兴发挥了一下。

922
00:47:22.980 --> 00:47:25.680
And my memory is that I improvise that.
我的记忆是，那是我即兴说的。

923
00:47:25.840 --> 00:47:30.400
And when I listened to the DVD commentary, Dave Rogers said, I'm pretty sure Angela improvised that line.
当我听DVD评论音轨时，戴夫·罗杰斯说，我很确定那是安吉拉即兴加的台词。

924
00:47:30.780 --> 00:47:34.900
So I just figured she would just be consumed with her own power.
我只是觉得她当时应该沉浸在自己的权力欲中。

925
00:47:34.900 --> 00:47:39.540
And, you know, Dwight has said if he if he takes over, she's gets to be in charge of the women.
而且，你知道，德怀特说过如果他接管公司，她就能负责管辖女性员工。

926
00:47:39.720 --> 00:47:41.220
So it's sort of a callback.
所以这算是一种呼应。

927
00:47:42.200 --> 00:47:45.700
And, you know, Kelly Kapoor has been on her list for a long time.
而且，凯莉·卡普尔在她的黑名单上已经很久了。

928
00:47:46.080 --> 00:47:49.020
Well, I think this is also a callback to product recall.
嗯，我觉得这也呼应了“产品召回”那一集。

929
00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:55.340
I think that Kelly went to the top of Angela's list after she had to sit through that customer service training.
我觉得凯莉是在被迫参加完那次客户服务培训后，才登上了安吉拉的黑名单榜首的。

930
00:47:55.600 --> 00:47:56.320
Well, no doubt.
毫无疑问。

931
00:47:56.500 --> 00:47:56.960
No doubt.
确实。

932
00:47:57.120 --> 00:47:59.200
She tried to kiss Dwight at a Christmas party.
她曾在圣诞派对上试图亲吻德怀特。

933
00:48:00.020 --> 00:48:03.320
And then there was Diwali and then product recall.
然后还有排灯节，接着就是产品召回事件。

934
00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:05.880
So Angela's like, see you later, Kelly Kapoor.
所以安吉拉才会说，走着瞧吧，凯莉·卡普尔。

935
00:48:06.280 --> 00:48:06.460
Yeah.
没错。

936
00:48:06.740 --> 00:48:08.280
Who's next on Angela's list?
安吉拉名单上的下一个是谁？

937
00:48:08.400 --> 00:48:09.640
The list is long, lady.
名单很长呢，女士。

938
00:48:09.880 --> 00:48:10.640
The list is long.
名单很长。

939
00:48:10.880 --> 00:48:10.940
Is it Kevin?
是凯文吗？

940
00:48:11.520 --> 00:48:12.260
Maybe Kevin.
可能是凯文。

941
00:48:12.500 --> 00:48:13.680
Oh, for sure.
哦，肯定的。

942
00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:14.620
For sure.
绝对是。

943
00:48:15.660 --> 00:48:17.460
And maybe she gets her way in the finale.
也许她在结局里就如愿以偿了。

944
00:48:17.460 --> 00:48:19.460
Just saying, OK, we're not there yet.
我只是随口一说，好吧，我们还没到那儿呢。

945
00:48:19.840 --> 00:48:24.280
OK, well, in the scene, Dwight and Angela have this really fun couplet of dialogue.
好吧，在这一幕里，德怀特和安吉拉有一段非常有趣的对话。

946
00:48:25.140 --> 00:48:29.180
Dwight says, how would you like to spend the night with a regional manager of Dunder Mifflin's?
德怀特说：“你想和邓德·米夫林的区域经理共度良宵吗？”

947
00:48:29.200 --> 00:48:31.000
And Angela goes, no, Dwight.
然后安吉拉说：“不，德怀特。”

948
00:48:31.180 --> 00:48:34.820
And I don't care if that's how they consolidated power in ancient Rome.
“我才不管古罗马是不是这么巩固权力的。”

949
00:48:35.940 --> 00:48:37.820
And he's like, I mean me.
然后他说：“我是说我。”

950
00:48:39.200 --> 00:48:42.540
Well, listen, lady, I think maybe we should take a break.
好吧，听着，女士，我觉得我们或许该休息一下了。

951
00:48:42.540 --> 00:48:48.680
And when we come back, we're going to see what this new power does to Dwight.
广告回来后，我们将看看这种新权力会对德怀特产生什么影响。

952
00:48:49.720 --> 00:48:52.400
Oh, well, get ready.
哦，好吧，做好准备吧。

953
00:48:52.580 --> 00:48:54.660
Get ready for his bed and breakfast in hell.
为他在地狱里的民宿做好准备吧。

954
00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:56.780
All right.
好的。

955
00:48:57.040 --> 00:48:58.160
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

956
00:48:58.160 --> 00:49:07.570
All right.
好的。

957
00:49:07.830 --> 00:49:08.590
We are back.
我们回来了。

958
00:49:08.850 --> 00:49:15.230
And Dwight is taunting Jim about his new position at Hotel Hell.
德怀特正在嘲讽吉姆，说他在“地狱旅馆”的新职位。

959
00:49:15.670 --> 00:49:19.770
And he's doing one of those hand, what are they called?
他还在用那个手部，那叫什么来着？

960
00:49:20.290 --> 00:49:22.030
Those hand exerciser things.
那种手部锻炼器。

961
00:49:22.270 --> 00:49:23.250
What are those for?
那是干什么用的？

962
00:49:23.410 --> 00:49:25.350
Why am I exercising my hand?
我为什么要锻炼手部？

963
00:49:25.530 --> 00:49:26.950
So your grip gets really strong.
这样你的握力会变得非常强。

964
00:49:26.950 --> 00:49:30.650
So I can hold heavier weights while I'm lifting weights.
这样我在举重时就能拿得动更重的杠铃了。

965
00:49:30.650 --> 00:49:31.830
Is that what that's for?
那是它的用途吗？

966
00:49:32.350 --> 00:49:33.110
Or maybe.
或者也许吧。

967
00:49:33.430 --> 00:49:34.750
What do I need a strong hand for?
我为什么需要强壮的手？

968
00:49:34.910 --> 00:49:38.630
Maybe if you wrestle, you can grab someone and hold real tight.
也许如果你摔跤的话，你可以抓住某人并紧紧握住。

969
00:49:38.950 --> 00:49:39.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

970
00:49:40.670 --> 00:49:41.410
I don't.
我不知道。

971
00:49:41.490 --> 00:49:46.350
I've never understood why I would want my hands to be super muscularly.
我从来没明白为什么我想要我的手变得肌肉发达。

972
00:49:46.970 --> 00:49:47.490
Muscularly?
肌肉发达？

973
00:49:47.630 --> 00:49:48.150
Muscular.
肌肉发达的。

974
00:49:48.470 --> 00:49:50.490
I feel like my husband has one.
我觉得我丈夫有一个。

975
00:49:50.710 --> 00:49:56.970
And I know with baking, like he's kneading all kinds of dough and bread and doing stuff.
我知道他喜欢烘焙，他会揉各种面团和面包之类的东西。

976
00:49:57.070 --> 00:49:59.770
And I feel like he's got real strong hands.
我觉得他的手真的很有力。

977
00:50:01.110 --> 00:50:02.570
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

978
00:50:02.690 --> 00:50:03.750
Do I knead one of those?
我需要一个那种东西吗？

979
00:50:03.910 --> 00:50:04.210
Maybe.
也许吧。

980
00:50:04.510 --> 00:50:05.810
So that I can knead my dough better?
这样我就能更好地揉面团了？

981
00:50:06.110 --> 00:50:06.530
Maybe.
也许吧。

982
00:50:06.530 --> 00:50:10.010
Then you'd have like super dough kneading strength.
那你就会拥有超级揉面力量了。

983
00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:11.590
Hmm.
嗯。

984
00:50:12.130 --> 00:50:12.450
Anyway.
总之。

985
00:50:12.570 --> 00:50:15.230
Maybe I should ask for one for Christmas.
也许我应该在圣诞节要一个。

986
00:50:16.030 --> 00:50:20.810
Dwight is doing this throughout this whole ridiculous, I don't even know what it is,
德怀特在整个荒谬的过程中都在做这个，我甚至不知道那是什么，

987
00:50:20.930 --> 00:50:24.250
a dream or fantasy of his, of this insane Hotel Hell.
是他关于这个疯狂的“地狱旅馆”的梦境或幻想。

988
00:50:24.430 --> 00:50:27.670
And then Jim just takes him to task so calmly.
然后吉姆非常冷静地质问他。

989
00:50:28.190 --> 00:50:29.370
He's like, wait, wait.
他说，等等，等等。

990
00:50:29.770 --> 00:50:30.550
You're the manager.
你是经理。

991
00:50:30.870 --> 00:50:31.090
You don't.
你不是。

992
00:50:31.190 --> 00:50:31.890
This is your fantasy.
这是你的幻想。

993
00:50:32.110 --> 00:50:32.770
You don't even own it.
你甚至不是它的老板。

994
00:50:32.850 --> 00:50:35.030
And he's like, I co-own it with Satan.
他说，我和撒旦共同拥有它。

995
00:50:36.190 --> 00:50:36.590
Yeah.
是啊。

996
00:50:36.870 --> 00:50:42.730
And he's like, I just want to make sure I'm clear that your wildest fantasy has you as
他说，我只是想确认一下，你最狂野的幻想竟然是

997
00:50:42.730 --> 00:50:46.330
the co-owner of a bed and breakfast with Satan in hell.
在地狱里和撒旦合伙开一家民宿。

998
00:50:46.810 --> 00:50:49.130
But you only make $80,000 a year.
但你一年只挣八万美元。

999
00:50:49.310 --> 00:50:49.510
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1000
00:50:49.590 --> 00:50:50.250
Dwight's like, wait, wait, wait.
德怀特说，等等，等等，等等。

1001
00:50:50.290 --> 00:50:51.310
I haven't told you the best part.
我还没告诉你最精彩的部分呢。

1002
00:50:52.310 --> 00:50:52.710
Yeah.
是吗。

1003
00:50:53.090 --> 00:50:53.510
The best part.
最精彩的部分。

1004
00:50:53.590 --> 00:50:54.990
I make $80,000 a year.
我年薪八万美元。

1005
00:50:55.550 --> 00:50:55.990
Now, Jenna.
好了，珍娜。

1006
00:50:56.710 --> 00:50:57.730
So here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1007
00:50:57.730 --> 00:51:05.890
I saw online that fans of The Office were like, you know, if you divide $80,000 by 12, you
我在网上看到《办公室》的粉丝们说，你知道，如果你把八万除以十二，你

1008
00:51:05.890 --> 00:51:10.470
get like 6666.666667 or something like that.
会得到六千六百六十六点六六六六六七之类的数字。

1009
00:51:10.570 --> 00:51:11.530
And I was like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

1010
00:51:11.630 --> 00:51:12.910
Do the writers do that on purpose?
编剧们是故意的吗？

1011
00:51:13.750 --> 00:51:14.730
They must have.
他们一定是故意的。

1012
00:51:14.770 --> 00:51:15.650
They had to have.
他们肯定是的。

1013
00:51:15.810 --> 00:51:16.050
They must have.
他们一定是。

1014
00:51:16.250 --> 00:51:19.210
Well, what a brilliant little layer they gave that then.
哇，那他们埋下的这个小细节真是太绝了。

1015
00:51:19.210 --> 00:51:21.110
We had a lot of people write in about that.
很多人写信给我们提到了这一点。

1016
00:51:21.230 --> 00:51:28.250
Rebecca Womack, Beth Jones, and Paulina Jay and Jake Moss all also noticed that $80,000
丽贝卡·沃马克、贝丝·琼斯、宝琳娜·杰伊和杰克·莫斯也都注意到了八万美元

1017
00:51:28.250 --> 00:51:31.750
a year is $6,666.66.
一年就是六千六百六十六点六六美元。

1018
00:51:32.430 --> 00:51:33.350
That's pretty cool.
这挺酷的。

1019
00:51:33.730 --> 00:51:34.650
I mean, that's a little.
我是说，这有点……

1020
00:51:34.810 --> 00:51:36.490
I mean, I like little details like that.
我是说，我喜欢这种小细节。

1021
00:51:36.590 --> 00:51:37.270
I think that's fun.
我觉得这很有趣。

1022
00:51:37.590 --> 00:51:42.110
You know, if that were my salary, I think I would be a little bit weirded out.
你知道，如果那是我的薪水，我想我会觉得有点怪怪的。

1023
00:51:42.270 --> 00:51:44.330
I don't think I would want to have a salary.
我觉得我不会想要那样的薪水。

1024
00:51:44.510 --> 00:51:45.610
I wouldn't want to get checks.
我可不想领那样的支票。

1025
00:51:45.610 --> 00:51:48.550
I mean, I guess you take out the taxes and everything.
我是说，我想你还得扣除税款什么的。

1026
00:51:48.870 --> 00:51:50.190
Your check wouldn't really say that.
你的支票上其实不会写那个数字。

1027
00:51:50.310 --> 00:51:52.690
But even still in my mind, I think it would weird me out.
但即便如此，我心里还是会觉得怪怪的。

1028
00:51:53.270 --> 00:51:56.050
Because do you know what I had for a very long time?
因为你知道我有一段时间一直用的是什么吗？

1029
00:51:57.190 --> 00:51:57.630
What?
什么？

1030
00:51:57.850 --> 00:51:58.030
What?
什么？

1031
00:51:58.830 --> 00:52:00.230
I had a credit card.
我有一张信用卡。

1032
00:52:00.430 --> 00:52:03.670
And you know, you have your little three digit secret code.
你知道，信用卡背面有那个三位数的安全码。

1033
00:52:05.150 --> 00:52:07.530
My secret code was 666.
我的安全码是666。

1034
00:52:08.050 --> 00:52:09.170
Oh, no, no, no.
噢，不，不，不。

1035
00:52:09.410 --> 00:52:10.390
I'd say get that away.
我会说快把它拿走。

1036
00:52:10.710 --> 00:52:12.130
I'm not having any of that.
我可不想沾上那种东西。

1037
00:52:12.630 --> 00:52:15.190
I would be on the phone trying to buy something.
我当时打电话买东西的时候。

1038
00:52:15.990 --> 00:52:18.050
Like, let's say I'm ordering a pizza.
比如，假设我在订披萨。

1039
00:52:18.350 --> 00:52:20.310
And they'd be like, what's your credit card number?
他们会问，你的信用卡号是多少？

1040
00:52:20.430 --> 00:52:22.110
And they'd be like, and the security code?
然后他们会问，安全码是多少？

1041
00:52:22.290 --> 00:52:26.810
And I would always be like, it's 666.
我总是会说，是666。

1042
00:52:27.350 --> 00:52:28.410
And what would they say?
那他们会说什么？

1043
00:52:29.490 --> 00:52:30.930
People would be like, what?
人们会说，什么？

1044
00:52:31.310 --> 00:52:32.390
They would laugh.
他们会笑。

1045
00:52:32.570 --> 00:52:35.590
It was, and I'd always have to be like, I know, I know.
确实，我总是不得不说，我知道，我知道。

1046
00:52:36.110 --> 00:52:41.310
And I wanted to like, just intentionally get rid of this card.
我当时就想，干脆故意把这张卡弄丢算了。

1047
00:52:41.430 --> 00:52:43.090
So they would issue me a new one on now.
这样他们就会给我换一张新的。

1048
00:52:43.190 --> 00:52:44.850
That's not my security code anymore.
现在那已经不是我的安全码了。

1049
00:52:45.110 --> 00:52:50.570
But I imagine that's like layered because it's like, on the one hand, that's creepy.
但我认为这就像是多重含义，一方面，这很诡异。

1050
00:52:50.850 --> 00:52:51.710
It's creepy.
这很诡异。

1051
00:52:51.930 --> 00:52:53.390
And then you have to say these creepy numbers.
然后你还得说出这些令人毛骨悚然的数字。

1052
00:52:53.390 --> 00:52:56.770
But then you also now have chitty chat.
但现在你还得闲聊。

